{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019H8tRhSRXJdFguAp7tpQV4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-16-1100-tune-gkr-precompute-m-parameters\n2\t\n3\tTune the GKR fractional sumcheck PrecomputeM strategy parameters (`TARGET_BLOCKS`, `MIN_BLOCKS`, `MIN_N`, `TAIL_TILE`) to reduce the GKR inner round cost at APC 300. The GKR inner rounds are the single largest sequential component at 213ms (107ms per segment), with `precompute_m_build_partial` at 45ms and `multifold` at 47ms being the dominant kernels. The current defaults (`TARGET_BLOCKS=1024`, `MIN_BLOCKS=64`, `MIN_N=22`, `TAIL_TILE=4096`) were set without specific tuning for the APC 300 workload, which has a different GKR tree shape (more traces, smaller per-trace) than APC 0. Parameter sweeping via the existing `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_*` environment variables can identify a configuration that better balances GPU parallelism and per-window overhead for this workload.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4e113b8-a396-45cc-8e86-654a475f0e59","uuid":"1564d8e9-b737-4097-8298-d4ceaa3f078b","timestamp":"2026-04-16T09:59:55.208Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-16-1100-tune-gkr-precompute-m-parameters\n\nTune the GKR fractional sumcheck PrecomputeM strategy parameters (`TARGET_BLOCKS`, `MIN_BLOCKS`, `MIN_N`, `TAIL_TILE`) to reduce the GKR inner round cost at APC 300. The GKR inner rounds are the single largest sequential component at 213ms (107ms per segment), with `precompute_m_build_partial` at 45ms and `multifold` at 47ms being the dominant kernels. The current defaults (`TARGET_BLOCKS=1024`, `MIN_BLOCKS=64`, `MIN_N=22`, `TAIL_TILE=4096`) were set without specific tuning for the APC 300 workload, which has a different GKR tree shape (more traces, smaller per-trace) than APC 0. Parameter sweeping via the existing `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_*` environment variables can identify a configuration that better balances GPU parallelism and per-window overhead for this workload.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
