{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S9URiMnHPmHMVLyEETkpGf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tuse std::{iter::zip, sync::Arc};\n2\t\n3\tuse itertools::Itertools;\n4\tuse openvm_cuda_common::{\n5\t    copy::{MemCopyD2H, MemCopyH2D},\n6\t    d_buffer::DeviceBuffer,\n7\t    memory_manager::MemTracker,\n8\t};\n9\tuse openvm_stark_backend::{\n10\t    proof::{MerkleProof, WhirProof},\n11\t    prover::MatrixDimensions,\n12\t    SystemParams,\n13\t};\n14\tuse p3_field::{BasedVectorSpace, PrimeCharacteristicRing, TwoAdicField};\n15\tuse p3_util::log2_strict_usize;\n16\tuse tracing::instrument;\n17\t\n18\tuse crate::{\n19\t    base::DeviceMatrix,\n20\t    cuda::{\n21\t        batch_ntt_small::batch_ntt_small,\n22\t        matrix::{batch_expand_pad, split_ext_to_base_col_major_matrix},\n23\t        mle_interpolate::mle_interpolate_stage_ext,\n24\t        poly::{eval_poly_ext_at_point_from_base, transpose_fp_to_fpext_vec},\n25\t        whir::{\n26\t            _whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_required_temp_buffer_size, w_moments_accumulate,\n27\t            whir_algebraic_batch_traces, whir_fold_coeffs_and_moments,\n28\t            whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_round,\n29\t        },\n30\t    },\n31\t    hash_scheme::GpuHashScheme,\n32\t    merkle_tree::{MerkleProofQueryDigest, MerkleTreeConstructor, MerkleTreeGpu},\n33\t    ntt::batch_ntt,\n34\t    poly::evals_eq_hypercube,\n35\t    prelude::{D_EF, EF, F},\n36\t    sponge::GpuFiatShamirTranscript,\n37\t    stacked_pcs::rs_code_matrix,\n38\t    stacked_reduction::StackedPcsData2,\n39\t    WhirProverError,\n40\t};\n41\t\n42\t#[repr(C)]\n43\tpub(crate) struct BatchingTracePacket {\n44\t    /// Pointer to trace device buffer\n45\t    ptr: *const F,\n46\t    /// Trace height\n47\t    height: u32,\n48\t    /// Trace width\n49\t    width: u32,\n50\t    /// Row start in the stacked matrix\n51\t    stacked_row_start: u32,\n52\t    /// Index in mu powers\n53\t    mu_idx: u32,\n54\t}\n55\t\n56\t#[instrument(\n57\t    name = \"prover.openings.whir\",\n58\t    level = \"info\",\n59\t    skip_all,\n60\t    fields(phase = \"prover\")\n61\t)]\n62\tpub fn prove_whir_opening_gpu<HS, TS>(\n63\t    params: &SystemParams,\n64\t    transcript: &mut TS,\n65\t    mut stacked_per_commit: Vec<StackedPcsData2<HS::Digest>>,\n66\t    u: &[EF],\n67\t) -> Result<WhirProof<HS::SC>, WhirProverError>\n68\twhere\n69\t    HS: GpuHashScheme,\n70\t    TS: GpuFiatShamirTranscript<HS::SC>,\n71\t    HS::MerkleHash: MerkleTreeConstructor,\n72\t    HS::Digest: MerkleProofQueryDigest,\n73\t{\n74\t    let mem = MemTracker::start(\"prover.prove_whir_opening\");\n75\t    let l_skip = params.l_skip;\n76\t    let log_blowup = params.log_blowup;\n77\t    let k_whir = params.k_whir();\n78\t    let whir_params = params.whir();\n79\t    let log_final_poly_len = params.log_final_poly_len();\n80\t\n81\t    let height = stacked_per_commit[0].layout().height();\n82\t    debug_assert!(stacked_per_commit\n83\t        .iter()\n84\t        .all(|d| d.layout().height() == height));\n85\t    let mut m = log2_strict_usize(height);\n86\t    assert_eq!(m, u.len());\n87\t    debug_assert!(m >= l_skip);\n88\t\n89\t    // Proof-of-work grinding before μ batching challenge.\n90\t    // This amplifies soundness of the initial batching step.\n91\t    let mu_pow_witness = transcript\n92\t        .grind_gpu(whir_params.mu_pow_bits)\n93\t        .map_err(WhirProverError::MuGrind)?;\n94\t    // Sample randomness for algebraic batching.\n95\t    // We batch the codewords for \\hat{q}_j together _before_ applying WHIR.\n96\t    let mu = transcript.sample_ext();\n97\t    let num_commits = stacked_per_commit.len();\n98\t\n99\t    // The coefficient table of `\\hat{f}` in the current WHIR round (MLE coefficient form).\n100\t    let mut f_ple_evals = DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(height * D_EF);\n101\t    // We algebraically batch all matrices together so we only need to interpolate one column vector\n102\t    {\n103\t        let mut packets = Vec::new();\n104\t        let mut total_stacked_width = 0u32;\n105\t        for stacked in &stacked_per_commit {\n106\t            let layout = stacked.layout();\n107\t            for (trace, &idx) in zip(&stacked.traces, &layout.mat_starts) {\n108\t                let (_, _, s) = layout.sorted_cols[idx];\n109\t                let packet = BatchingTracePacket {\n110\t                    ptr: trace.buffer().as_ptr(),\n111\t                    height: trace.height() as u32,\n112\t                    width: trace.width() as u32,\n113\t                    stacked_row_start: s.row_idx as u32,\n114\t                    mu_idx: total_stacked_width + s.col_idx as u32,\n115\t                };\n116\t                packets.push(packet);\n117\t            }\n118\t            total_stacked_width += layout.width() as u32;\n119\t        }\n120\t        let mu_powers = mu.powers().take(total_stacked_width as usize).collect_vec();\n121\t        let d_mu_powers = mu_powers.to_device()?;\n122\t        let d_packets = packets.to_device()?;\n123\t        // SAFETY:\n124\t        // - `mu_powers` has length `total_width`.\n125\t        // - `f_ple_evals` has capacity `height * D_EF` (stacked height in base coordinates).\n126\t        // - `d_packets` contain valid pointers and stacked row indices by construction.\n127\t        unsafe {\n128\t            whir_algebraic_batch_traces(&mut f_ple_evals, &d_packets, &d_mu_powers, 1 << l_skip)\n129\t                .map_err(WhirProverError::AlgebraicBatch)?;\n130\t        }\n131\t        for stacked in &mut stacked_per_commit {\n132\t            // drop traces to free device memory if RS codewords matrix exists\n133\t            if stacked.inner.tree.backing_matrix.is_some() {\n134\t                stacked.traces.clear();\n135\t            }\n136\t        }\n137\t    } // common_main_pcs_data.matrix has now been freed\n138\t\n139\t    // Compute \\hat{f} coefficients:\n140\t    //\n141\t    // Step 1: iDFT per chunk of size 2^l_skip. After this, each chunk holds univariate\n142\t    // coefficients c_z(x) of f(Z, x) for a fixed boolean assignment x in H_{m - l_skip}.\n143\t    unsafe {\n144\t        let num_poly = f_ple_evals.len() >> l_skip;\n145\t        batch_ntt_small(&mut f_ple_evals, l_skip, num_poly, true)\n146\t            .map_err(WhirProverError::CustomBatchIntt)?;\n147\t    }\n148\t    let mut f_coeffs = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(height);\n149\t    // SAFETY: `f_ple_evals` is constructed with length `height * D_EF`.\n150\t    unsafe {\n151\t        transpose_fp_to_fpext_vec(&mut f_coeffs, &f_ple_evals)\n152\t            .map_err(WhirProverError::Transpose)?;\n153\t    }\n154\t    drop(f_ple_evals);\n155\t    // Step 2: Within-chunk zeta (stages 0..l_skip). Applies the subset-zeta transform\n156\t    // over the Z-index bits, converting univariate coefficients (root-of-unity basis)\n157\t    // into hypercube evaluations over H_{l_skip}. Together with step 1, this computes\n158\t    // eval_to_coeff_rs_message, i.e. the MLE coefficient table of \\hat{f}.\n159\t    for i in 0..l_skip {\n160\t        let step = 1u32 << i;\n161\t        // SAFETY: `f_coeffs` has length `2^m` with `m >= l_skip`.\n162\t        unsafe {\n163\t            mle_interpolate_stage_ext(&mut f_coeffs, step, false)\n164\t                .map_err(|error| WhirProverError::MleInterpolate { error, step })?;\n165\t        }\n166\t    }\n167\t\n168\t    debug_assert_eq!((m - log_final_poly_len) % k_whir, 0);\n169\t    let num_whir_rounds = (m - log_final_poly_len) / k_whir;\n170\t    assert!(num_whir_rounds > 0);\n171\t\n172\t    // We maintain moments of \\hat{w}:\n173\t    // M[T] = sum_{x superset T} \\hat{w}(x).\n174\t    // For initial \\hat{w} = mobius_eq(u, -), these moments are exactly eq(u, -).\n175\t    let mut w_moments = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(1 << m);\n176\t    unsafe {\n177\t        evals_eq_hypercube(&mut w_moments, u).map_err(WhirProverError::EvalEq)?;\n178\t    }\n179\t\n180\t    let mut whir_sumcheck_polys: Vec<[EF; 2]> = vec![];\n181\t    let mut codeword_commits = vec![];\n182\t    let mut ood_values = vec![];\n183\t    // per commitment, per whir query, per column\n184\t    let mut initial_round_opened_rows: Vec<Vec<Vec<Vec<F>>>> = vec![vec![]; num_commits];\n185\t    let mut initial_round_merkle_proofs: Vec<Vec<MerkleProof<HS::Digest>>> = vec![];\n186\t    let mut codeword_opened_values: Vec<Vec<Vec<EF>>> = vec![];\n187\t    let mut codeword_merkle_proofs: Vec<Vec<MerkleProof<HS::Digest>>> = vec![];\n188\t    let mut folding_pow_witnesses = vec![];\n189\t    let mut query_phase_pow_witnesses = vec![];\n190\t    let mut rs_tree = None;\n191\t    let mut log_rs_domain_size = m + log_blowup;\n192\t    let mut final_poly = None;\n193\t\n194\t    let mut d_s_evals = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(2);\n195\t    let mut d_sumcheck_tmp = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::new();\n196\t\n197\t    mem.tracing_info(\"before_whir_rounds\");\n198\t    // We will drop `stacked_per_commit` and hence `common_main_pcs_data` after whir round 0.\n199\t    for (whir_round, round_params) in whir_params.rounds.iter().enumerate() {\n200\t        let is_last_round = whir_round == num_whir_rounds - 1;\n201\t        // Run k_whir rounds of sumcheck on `sum_{x in H_m} \\hat{w}(\\hat{f}(x), x)`\n202\t        for round in 0..k_whir {\n203\t            // Do not use f_coeffs.len() because it might have extra capacity.\n204\t            let f_height = 1 << (m - round);\n205\t            debug_assert!(\n206\t                f_coeffs.len() >= f_height,\n207\t                \"f_coeffs has length {}, expected 2^{} for m={m}, round={round}\",\n208\t                f_coeffs.len(),\n209\t                m - round\n210\t            );\n211\t            debug_assert!(w_moments.len() >= f_height);\n212\t            let output_height = f_height / 2;\n213\t            let tmp_buffer_capacity =\n214\t                unsafe { _whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_required_temp_buffer_size(f_height as u32) };\n215\t            if d_sumcheck_tmp.len() < tmp_buffer_capacity as usize {\n216\t                d_sumcheck_tmp = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(tmp_buffer_capacity as usize);\n217\t            }\n218\t            let mut new_f_coeffs = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(output_height);\n219\t            let mut new_w_moments = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(output_height);\n220\t            // SAFETY:\n221\t            // - `d_s_evals` has length 2\n222\t            // - `d_sumcheck_tmp` has at least required scratch length\n223\t            unsafe {\n224\t                whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_round(\n225\t                    &f_coeffs,\n226\t                    &w_moments,\n227\t                    &mut d_s_evals,\n228\t                    &mut d_sumcheck_tmp,\n229\t                    f_height as u32,\n230\t                )\n231\t                .map_err(|error| WhirProverError::SumcheckMleRound {\n232\t                    error,\n233\t                    whir_round,\n234\t                    round,\n235\t                })?;\n236\t            }\n237\t            let s_evals = d_s_evals.to_host()?;\n238\t            for &eval in &s_evals {\n239\t                transcript.observe_ext(eval);\n240\t            }\n241\t            whir_sumcheck_polys.push(s_evals.try_into().unwrap());\n242\t\n243\t            folding_pow_witnesses.push(\n244\t                transcript\n245\t                    .grind_gpu(whir_params.folding_pow_bits)\n246\t                    .map_err(WhirProverError::FoldingGrind)?,\n247\t            );\n248\t            let alpha = transcript.sample_ext();\n249\t\n250\t            // Fold `f` and `w` in coefficient/moment form with respect to `alpha`.\n251\t            // SAFETY:\n252\t            // - input buffers have length `f_height`.\n253\t            // - output buffers have length `f_height / 2`.\n254\t            unsafe {\n255\t                whir_fold_coeffs_and_moments(\n256\t                    &f_coeffs,\n257\t                    &w_moments,\n258\t                    &mut new_f_coeffs,\n259\t                    &mut new_w_moments,\n260\t                    alpha,\n261\t                    f_height as u32,\n262\t                )\n263\t                .map_err(|error| WhirProverError::FoldMle {\n264\t                    error,\n265\t                    whir_round,\n266\t                    round,\n267\t                })?;\n268\t            }\n269\t            f_coeffs = new_f_coeffs;\n270\t            w_moments = new_w_moments;\n271\t        }\n272\t        // Define g^ = f^(alpha, \\cdot) and send matrix commit of RS(g^)\n273\t        // `f_coeffs` is the coefficient form of f^(alpha, \\cdot).\n274\t        let f_height = 1 << (m - k_whir);\n275\t        debug_assert!(f_coeffs.len() >= f_height);\n276\t        debug_assert_eq!(size_of::<EF>() / size_of::<F>(), D_EF);\n277\t        let mut g_coeffs = DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(f_height * D_EF);\n278\t        // SAFETY: we allocated `f_coeffs.len() * D_EF` space for `g_coeffs` to do a 1-to-D_EF\n279\t        // (1-to-4) split\n280\t        unsafe {\n281\t            split_ext_to_base_col_major_matrix(\n282\t                &mut g_coeffs,\n283\t                &f_coeffs,\n284\t                f_height as u64,\n285\t                f_height as u32,\n286\t            )\n287\t            .map_err(|error| WhirProverError::SplitExtPoly { error, whir_round })?;\n288\t        }\n289\t        let (g_tree, z_0) = if !is_last_round {\n290\t            let codeword_height = 1 << (log_rs_domain_size - 1);\n291\t            // `g: \\mathcal{L}^{(2)} \\to \\mathbb F`\n292\t            let g_rs = DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(D_EF * codeword_height);\n293\t            // SAFETY:\n294\t            // - g_coeffs is a single EF polynomial, treated as 4 F-polynomials of height\n295\t            //   2^{m-k_whir}\n296\t            // - We resize each F-poly to RS domain size 2^{log_rs_domain_size - 1}, which is\n297\t            //   equivalent to resizing the EF-polynomial\n298\t            unsafe {\n299\t                batch_expand_pad(\n300\t                    g_rs.as_mut_ptr(),\n301\t                    g_coeffs.as_ptr(),\n302\t                    D_EF as u32,\n303\t                    codeword_height as u32,\n304\t                    f_height as u32,\n305\t                )\n306\t                .map_err(|error| WhirProverError::BatchExpandPad { error, whir_round })?;\n307\t\n308\t                batch_ntt(\n309\t                    &g_rs,\n310\t                    (log_rs_domain_size - 1) as u32,\n311\t                    0u32,\n312\t                    D_EF as u32,\n313\t                    true,\n314\t                    false,\n315\t                );\n316\t            }\n317\t\n318\t            let g_tree = MerkleTreeGpu::<F, HS::Digest>::new_with_hash::<HS::MerkleHash>(\n319\t                DeviceMatrix::new(Arc::new(g_rs), codeword_height, D_EF),\n320\t                1 << k_whir,\n321\t                true,\n322\t            )\n323\t            .map_err(WhirProverError::MerkleTree)?;\n324\t            let g_commit = g_tree.root();\n325\t            transcript.observe_commit(g_commit);\n326\t            codeword_commits.push(g_commit);\n327\t\n328\t            let z_0 = transcript.sample_ext();\n329\t            // SAFETY:\n330\t            // - `g_coeffs` is coefficient form of `\\hat{g}`, which is degree `2^{m-k_whir}`.\n331\t            // - `g_coeffs` is F-column major matrix.\n332\t            let g_opened_value = unsafe {\n333\t                eval_poly_ext_at_point_from_base(&g_coeffs, 1 << (m - k_whir), z_0)\n334\t                    .map_err(|error| WhirProverError::EvalPolyAtPoint { error, whir_round })?\n335\t            };\n336\t            transcript.observe_ext(g_opened_value);\n337\t            ood_values.push(g_opened_value);\n338\t\n339\t            (Some(g_tree), Some(z_0))\n340\t        } else {\n341\t            // Observe the final poly\n342\t            debug_assert_eq!(log_final_poly_len, m - k_whir);\n343\t            let final_poly_len = 1 << log_final_poly_len;\n344\t            let base_coeffs = g_coeffs.to_host()?;\n345\t            debug_assert_eq!(base_coeffs.len(), D_EF * final_poly_len);\n346\t            let mut coeffs = Vec::with_capacity(final_poly_len);\n347\t            for i in 0..final_poly_len {\n348\t                let coeff = EF::from_basis_coefficients_fn(|j| base_coeffs[j * final_poly_len + i]);\n349\t                transcript.observe_ext(coeff);\n350\t                coeffs.push(coeff);\n351\t            }\n352\t            final_poly = Some(coeffs);\n353\t            (None, None)\n354\t        };\n355\t\n356\t        // omega is generator of RS domain `\\mathcal{L}^{(2^k)}`\n357\t        let omega = F::two_adic_generator(log_rs_domain_size - k_whir);\n358\t        let num_queries = round_params.num_queries;\n359\t        let mut query_indices = Vec::with_capacity(num_queries);\n360\t        query_phase_pow_witnesses.push(\n361\t            transcript\n362\t                .grind_gpu(whir_params.query_phase_pow_bits)\n363\t                .map_err(WhirProverError::QueryPhaseGrind)?,\n364\t        );\n365\t        // Sample query indices first\n366\t        for _ in 0..num_queries {\n367\t            // This is the index of the leaf in the Merkle tree\n368\t            let index = transcript.sample_bits(log_rs_domain_size - k_whir);\n369\t            query_indices.push(index as usize);\n370\t        }\n371\t        if !is_last_round {\n372\t            codeword_opened_values.push(vec![]);\n373\t            codeword_merkle_proofs.push(vec![]);\n374\t        }\n375\t        if whir_round == 0 {\n376\t            // Vector to hold owned copies of backing matrices that are regenerated in the case they\n377\t            // were not cached\n378\t            let mut backing_mats_owned = vec![None; stacked_per_commit.len()];\n379\t            let mut backing_matrices = Vec::with_capacity(stacked_per_commit.len());\n380\t            let mut trees = Vec::with_capacity(stacked_per_commit.len());\n381\t            for (d, backing_mat_owned) in zip(&mut stacked_per_commit, &mut backing_mats_owned) {\n382\t                trees.push(&d.inner.tree);\n383\t                if let Some(matrix) = d.inner.tree.backing_matrix.as_ref() {\n384\t                    backing_matrices.push(matrix);\n385\t                } else {\n386\t                    let layout = d.layout();\n387\t                    let traces = d.traces.iter().collect_vec();\n388\t                    debug_assert!(!traces.is_empty());\n389\t                    let backing_matrix =\n390\t                        rs_code_matrix(log_blowup, layout, &traces, &d.inner.matrix)\n391\t                            .map_err(WhirProverError::RsCodeMatrix)?;\n392\t                    d.traces.clear();\n393\t                    *backing_mat_owned = Some(backing_matrix);\n394\t                    backing_matrices.push(backing_mat_owned.as_ref().unwrap());\n395\t                }\n396\t            }\n397\t            // Get merkle proofs for in-domain samples necessary to evaluate Fold(f, \\vec\n398\t            // \\alpha)(z_i)\n399\t            initial_round_merkle_proofs =\n400\t                <MerkleTreeGpu<F, HS::Digest>>::batch_query_merkle_proofs(\n401\t                    trees.as_slice(),\n402\t                    &query_indices,\n403\t                )\n404\t                .map_err(WhirProverError::MerkleTree)?;\n405\t\n406\t            let query_stride = trees[0].query_stride();\n407\t            debug_assert!(\n408\t                trees.iter().all(|tree| tree.query_stride() == query_stride),\n409\t                \"Merkle trees don't have same layer size\"\n410\t            );\n411\t            let num_rows_per_query = trees[0].rows_per_query;\n412\t            debug_assert!(\n413\t                trees\n414\t                    .iter()\n415\t                    .all(|tree| tree.rows_per_query == num_rows_per_query),\n416\t                \"Merkle trees don't have same rows_per_query\"\n417\t            );\n418\t\n419\t            initial_round_opened_rows = MerkleTreeGpu::<F, HS::Digest>::batch_open_rows(\n420\t                &backing_matrices,\n421\t                &query_indices,\n422\t                query_stride,\n423\t                num_rows_per_query,\n424\t            )\n425\t            .map_err(WhirProverError::MerkleTree)?\n426\t            .into_iter()\n427\t            .map(|rows_per_commit| {\n428\t                rows_per_commit\n429\t                    .into_iter()\n430\t                    .map(|rows| {\n431\t                        let width = rows.len() / num_rows_per_query;\n432\t                        rows.chunks_exact(width).map(|row| row.to_vec()).collect()\n433\t                    })\n434\t                    .collect()\n435\t            })\n436\t            .collect();\n437\t            debug_assert_eq!(\n438\t                Arc::strong_count(&stacked_per_commit[0].inner),\n439\t                1,\n440\t                \"common_main_pcs_data should be owned\"\n441\t            );\n442\t            stacked_per_commit.clear(); // this drops common_main_pcs_data\n443\t            mem.tracing_info(\"after_initial_whir_round\");\n444\t        } else {\n445\t            let tree: &MerkleTreeGpu<F, HS::Digest> = rs_tree.as_ref().unwrap();\n446\t            codeword_merkle_proofs[whir_round - 1] =\n447\t                <MerkleTreeGpu<F, HS::Digest>>::batch_query_merkle_proofs(&[tree], &query_indices)\n448\t                    .map_err(WhirProverError::MerkleTree)?\n449\t                    .pop()\n450\t                    .expect(\"exactly 1 tree\");\n451\t            codeword_opened_values[whir_round - 1] =\n452\t                MerkleTreeGpu::<F, HS::Digest>::batch_open_rows(\n453\t                    &[tree.backing_matrix.as_ref().unwrap()],\n454\t                    &query_indices,\n455\t                    tree.query_stride(),\n456\t                    tree.rows_per_query,\n457\t                )\n458\t                .map_err(WhirProverError::MerkleTree)?\n459\t                .pop()\n460\t                .unwrap()\n461\t                .into_iter()\n462\t                .map(EF::reconstitute_from_base)\n463\t                .collect();\n464\t        }\n465\t        rs_tree = g_tree;\n466\t\n467\t        // We still sample on the last round to match the verifier, who uses a\n468\t        // final gamma to unify some logic. But we do not need to update\n469\t        // `w_moments`.\n470\t        let gamma = transcript.sample_ext();\n471\t\n472\t        if !is_last_round {\n473\t            // Update moments of \\hat{w}:\n474\t            // M(T) += gamma * z0^T + sum_i gamma^{i+1} * z_i^T.\n475\t            let log_height = (m - k_whir) as u32;\n476\t            let z0 = z_0.unwrap();\n477\t            let z_points = query_indices\n478\t                .iter()\n479\t                .map(|&index| omega.exp_u64(index as u64))\n480\t                .collect_vec();\n481\t\n482\t            let mut z0_pows2 = Vec::with_capacity(log_height as usize);\n483\t            let mut z0_pow = z0;\n484\t            for _ in 0..log_height {\n485\t                z0_pows2.push(z0_pow);\n486\t                z0_pow = z0_pow.square();\n487\t            }\n488\t\n489\t            let mut z_pows2 = Vec::with_capacity(num_queries * log_height as usize);\n490\t            for z in &z_points {\n491\t                let mut z_pow = *z;\n492\t                for _ in 0..log_height {\n493\t                    z_pows2.push(z_pow);\n494\t                    z_pow = z_pow.square();\n495\t                }\n496\t            }\n497\t\n498\t            let d_z0_pows2 = z0_pows2.to_device()?;\n499\t            let d_z_pows2 = z_pows2.to_device()?;\n500\t            unsafe {\n501\t                w_moments_accumulate(\n502\t                    &mut w_moments,\n503\t                    &d_z0_pows2,\n504\t                    &d_z_pows2,\n505\t                    gamma,\n506\t                    num_queries as u32,\n507\t                    log_height,\n508\t                )\n509\t                .map_err(|error| WhirProverError::WMomentsAccumulate { error, whir_round })?;\n510\t            }\n511\t        }\n512\t\n513\t        m -= k_whir;\n514\t        log_rs_domain_size -= 1;\n515\t    }\n516\t\n517\t    mem.emit_metrics();\n518\t    Ok(WhirProof {\n519\t        mu_pow_witness,\n520\t        whir_sumcheck_polys,\n521\t        codeword_commits,\n522\t        ood_values,\n523\t        folding_pow_witnesses,\n524\t        query_phase_pow_witnesses,\n525\t        initial_round_opened_rows,\n526\t        initial_round_merkle_proofs,\n527\t        codeword_opened_values,\n528\t        codeword_merkle_proofs,\n529\t        final_poly: final_poly.unwrap(),\n530\t    })\n531\t}\n532\t\n533\t#[cfg(test)]\n534\tmod tests {\n535\t    use std::sync::Arc;\n536\t\n537\t    use itertools::Itertools;\n538\t    use openvm_stark_backend::{\n539\t        keygen::types::MultiStarkProvingKey,\n540\t        prover::{\n541\t            stacked_pcs::stacked_commit, CpuColMajorBackend, DeviceDataTransporter, ProvingContext,\n542\t        },\n543\t        test_utils::{FibFixture, TestFixture},\n544\t        verifier::whir::{verify_whir, VerifyWhirError},\n545\t        StarkEngine, StarkProtocolConfig, SystemParams, WhirConfig, WhirParams,\n546\t        WhirProximityStrategy,\n547\t    };\n548\t    use openvm_stark_sdk::{\n549\t        config::{\n550\t            baby_bear_poseidon2::{\n551\t                default_duplex_sponge, BabyBearPoseidon2RefEngine, DuplexSponge,\n552\t            },\n553\t            log_up_params::log_up_security_params_baby_bear_100_bits,\n554\t        },\n555\t        utils::setup_tracing_with_log_level,\n556\t    };\n557\t    use rand::{rngs::StdRng, SeedableRng};\n558\t    use test_case::test_case;\n559\t    use tracing::Level;\n560\t\n561\t    use crate::{\n562\t        prelude::SC, sponge::DuplexSpongeGpu, stacked_reduction::StackedPcsData2,\n563\t        whir::prove_whir_opening_gpu, BabyBearPoseidon2GpuEngine, GpuBackend,\n564\t    };\n565\t\n566\t    /// GPU-specific WHIR test runner. Uses `prove_whir_opening_gpu` for the\n567\t    /// proving step and the shared CPU verifier for verification.\n568\t    fn run_whir_test_gpu(\n569\t        params: SystemParams,\n570\t        pk: MultiStarkProvingKey<SC>,\n571\t        ctx: ProvingContext<CpuColMajorBackend<SC>>,\n572\t    ) -> Result<(), VerifyWhirError> {\n573\t        let engine = BabyBearPoseidon2GpuEngine::new(params.clone());\n574\t        let device = engine.device();\n575\t        let mut rng = StdRng::seed_from_u64(0);\n576\t        let (z_prism, z_cube) = openvm_backend_tests::generate_random_z(&params, &mut rng);\n577\t\n578\t        let common_main_traces = ctx\n579\t            .common_main_traces()\n580\t            .map(|(_, trace)| trace)\n581\t            .collect_vec();\n582\t        // Use CPU stacked_commit to isolate GPU testing to WHIR prover\n583\t        let (common_main_commit, common_main_pcs_data) = stacked_commit(\n584\t            engine.config().hasher(),\n585\t            params.l_skip,\n586\t            params.n_stack,\n587\t            params.log_blowup,\n588\t            params.k_whir(),\n589\t            &common_main_traces,\n590\t        )\n591\t        .unwrap();\n592\t        let d_common_main_traces = common_main_traces\n593\t            .iter()\n594\t            .map(|t| {\n595\t                <_ as DeviceDataTransporter<SC, GpuBackend>>::transport_matrix_to_device(device, t)\n596\t            })\n597\t            .collect_vec();\n598\t        let d_common_main_pcs_data =\n599\t            <_ as DeviceDataTransporter<SC, GpuBackend>>::transport_pcs_data_to_device(\n600\t                device,\n601\t                &common_main_pcs_data,\n602\t            );\n603\t\n604\t        let mut stacking_openings = vec![openvm_backend_tests::stacking_openings_for_matrix(\n605\t            &params,\n606\t            &z_prism,\n607\t            &common_main_pcs_data.matrix,\n608\t        )];\n609\t        let mut commits = vec![common_main_commit];\n610\t        let mut stacked_per_commit = vec![StackedPcsData2 {\n611\t            inner: Arc::new(d_common_main_pcs_data),\n612\t            traces: d_common_main_traces,\n613\t        }];\n614\t        for (air_id, air_ctx) in ctx.per_trace {\n615\t            for data in pk.per_air[air_id]\n616\t                .preprocessed_data\n617\t                .iter()\n618\t                .chain(air_ctx.cached_mains.iter().map(|cd| &cd.data))\n619\t            {\n620\t                let trace =\n621\t                    <_ as DeviceDataTransporter<SC, GpuBackend>>::transport_matrix_to_device(\n622\t                        device,\n623\t                        &data.mat_view(0).to_matrix(),\n624\t                    );\n625\t                commits.push(data.commit().unwrap());\n626\t                stacking_openings.push(openvm_backend_tests::stacking_openings_for_matrix(\n627\t                    &params,\n628\t                    &z_prism,\n629\t                    &data.matrix,\n630\t                ));\n631\t                let d_data =\n632\t                    <_ as DeviceDataTransporter<SC, GpuBackend>>::transport_pcs_data_to_device(\n633\t                        device, data,\n634\t                    );\n635\t                stacked_per_commit.push(StackedPcsData2 {\n636\t                    inner: Arc::new(d_data),\n637\t                    traces: vec![trace],\n638\t                });\n639\t            }\n640\t        }\n641\t\n642\t        let mut prover_sponge = DuplexSpongeGpu::default();\n643\t\n644\t        let proof = prove_whir_opening_gpu::<crate::DefaultHashScheme, _>(\n645\t            &params,\n646\t            &mut prover_sponge,\n647\t            stacked_per_commit,\n648\t            &z_cube,\n649\t        )\n650\t        .unwrap();\n651\t\n652\t        let mut verifier_sponge = default_duplex_sponge();\n653\t        verify_whir(\n654\t            &mut verifier_sponge,\n655\t            engine.config(),\n656\t            &proof,\n657\t            &stacking_openings,\n658\t            &commits,\n659\t            &z_cube,\n660\t        )\n661\t    }\n662\t\n663\t    fn run_whir_fib_test_gpu(params: SystemParams) -> Result<(), VerifyWhirError> {\n664\t        let engine = BabyBearPoseidon2RefEngine::<DuplexSponge>::new(params.clone());\n665\t        let fib = FibFixture::new(0, 1, 1 << params.log_stacked_height());\n666\t        let (pk, _vk) = fib.keygen(&engine);\n667\t        let ctx = fib.generate_proving_ctx();\n668\t        run_whir_test_gpu(params, pk, ctx)\n669\t    }\n670\t\n671\t    fn whir_test_params(k_whir: usize, log_final_poly_len: usize) -> WhirParams {\n672\t        WhirParams {\n673\t            k: k_whir,\n674\t            log_final_poly_len,\n675\t            query_phase_pow_bits: 2,\n676\t            folding_pow_bits: 1,\n677\t            mu_pow_bits: 3,\n678\t            proximity: WhirProximityStrategy::UniqueDecoding,\n679\t        }\n680\t    }\n681\t\n682\t    #[test_case(0, 1, 1, 0)]\n683\t    #[test_case(2, 1, 1, 2)]\n684\t    #[test_case(2, 1, 2, 0)]\n685\t    #[test_case(2, 1, 3, 1)]\n686\t    #[test_case(2, 1, 4, 0)]\n687\t    #[test_case(2, 2, 4, 0)]\n688\t    fn test_whir_single_fib_gpu(\n689\t        n_stack: usize,\n690\t        log_blowup: usize,\n691\t        k_whir: usize,\n692\t        log_final_poly_len: usize,\n693\t    ) -> Result<(), VerifyWhirError> {\n694\t        setup_tracing_with_log_level(Level::DEBUG);\n695\t\n696\t        let l_skip = 2;\n697\t        let w_stack = 8;\n698\t        let whir = WhirConfig::new(\n699\t            log_blowup,\n700\t            l_skip + n_stack,\n701\t            whir_test_params(k_whir, log_final_poly_len),\n702\t            10,\n703\t        );\n704\t        let params = SystemParams {\n705\t            l_skip: 2,\n706\t            n_stack,\n707\t            w_stack,\n708\t            log_blowup,\n709\t            whir,\n710\t            logup: log_up_security_params_baby_bear_100_bits(),\n711\t            max_constraint_degree: 3,\n712\t        };\n713\t        run_whir_fib_test_gpu(params)\n714\t    }\n715\t\n716\t    // TODO: test multiple commitments with GPU prover\n717\t}\n718\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4e113b8-a396-45cc-8e86-654a475f0e59","uuid":"295b0beb-8134-48dc-a550-879f7523a5b8","timestamp":"2026-04-16T10:13:29.011Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/whir.rs","content":"use std::{iter::zip, sync::Arc};\n\nuse itertools::Itertools;\nuse openvm_cuda_common::{\n    copy::{MemCopyD2H, MemCopyH2D},\n    d_buffer::DeviceBuffer,\n    memory_manager::MemTracker,\n};\nuse openvm_stark_backend::{\n    proof::{MerkleProof, WhirProof},\n    prover::MatrixDimensions,\n    SystemParams,\n};\nuse p3_field::{BasedVectorSpace, PrimeCharacteristicRing, TwoAdicField};\nuse p3_util::log2_strict_usize;\nuse tracing::instrument;\n\nuse crate::{\n    base::DeviceMatrix,\n    cuda::{\n        batch_ntt_small::batch_ntt_small,\n        matrix::{batch_expand_pad, split_ext_to_base_col_major_matrix},\n        mle_interpolate::mle_interpolate_stage_ext,\n        poly::{eval_poly_ext_at_point_from_base, transpose_fp_to_fpext_vec},\n        whir::{\n            _whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_required_temp_buffer_size, w_moments_accumulate,\n            whir_algebraic_batch_traces, whir_fold_coeffs_and_moments,\n            whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_round,\n        },\n    },\n    hash_scheme::GpuHashScheme,\n    merkle_tree::{MerkleProofQueryDigest, MerkleTreeConstructor, MerkleTreeGpu},\n    ntt::batch_ntt,\n    poly::evals_eq_hypercube,\n    prelude::{D_EF, EF, F},\n    sponge::GpuFiatShamirTranscript,\n    stacked_pcs::rs_code_matrix,\n    stacked_reduction::StackedPcsData2,\n    WhirProverError,\n};\n\n#[repr(C)]\npub(crate) struct BatchingTracePacket {\n    /// Pointer to trace device buffer\n    ptr: *const F,\n    /// Trace height\n    height: u32,\n    /// Trace width\n    width: u32,\n    /// Row start in the stacked matrix\n    stacked_row_start: u32,\n    /// Index in mu powers\n    mu_idx: u32,\n}\n\n#[instrument(\n    name = \"prover.openings.whir\",\n    level = \"info\",\n    skip_all,\n    fields(phase = \"prover\")\n)]\npub fn prove_whir_opening_gpu<HS, TS>(\n    params: &SystemParams,\n    transcript: &mut TS,\n    mut stacked_per_commit: Vec<StackedPcsData2<HS::Digest>>,\n    u: &[EF],\n) -> Result<WhirProof<HS::SC>, WhirProverError>\nwhere\n    HS: GpuHashScheme,\n    TS: GpuFiatShamirTranscript<HS::SC>,\n    HS::MerkleHash: MerkleTreeConstructor,\n    HS::Digest: MerkleProofQueryDigest,\n{\n    let mem = MemTracker::start(\"prover.prove_whir_opening\");\n    let l_skip = params.l_skip;\n    let log_blowup = params.log_blowup;\n    let k_whir = params.k_whir();\n    let whir_params = params.whir();\n    let log_final_poly_len = params.log_final_poly_len();\n\n    let height = stacked_per_commit[0].layout().height();\n    debug_assert!(stacked_per_commit\n        .iter()\n        .all(|d| d.layout().height() == height));\n    let mut m = log2_strict_usize(height);\n    assert_eq!(m, u.len());\n    debug_assert!(m >= l_skip);\n\n    // Proof-of-work grinding before μ batching challenge.\n    // This amplifies soundness of the initial batching step.\n    let mu_pow_witness = transcript\n        .grind_gpu(whir_params.mu_pow_bits)\n        .map_err(WhirProverError::MuGrind)?;\n    // Sample randomness for algebraic batching.\n    // We batch the codewords for \\hat{q}_j together _before_ applying WHIR.\n    let mu = transcript.sample_ext();\n    let num_commits = stacked_per_commit.len();\n\n    // The coefficient table of `\\hat{f}` in the current WHIR round (MLE coefficient form).\n    let mut f_ple_evals = DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(height * D_EF);\n    // We algebraically batch all matrices together so we only need to interpolate one column vector\n    {\n        let mut packets = Vec::new();\n        let mut total_stacked_width = 0u32;\n        for stacked in &stacked_per_commit {\n            let layout = stacked.layout();\n            for (trace, &idx) in zip(&stacked.traces, &layout.mat_starts) {\n                let (_, _, s) = layout.sorted_cols[idx];\n                let packet = BatchingTracePacket {\n                    ptr: trace.buffer().as_ptr(),\n                    height: trace.height() as u32,\n                    width: trace.width() as u32,\n                    stacked_row_start: s.row_idx as u32,\n                    mu_idx: total_stacked_width + s.col_idx as u32,\n                };\n                packets.push(packet);\n            }\n            total_stacked_width += layout.width() as u32;\n        }\n        let mu_powers = mu.powers().take(total_stacked_width as usize).collect_vec();\n        let d_mu_powers = mu_powers.to_device()?;\n        let d_packets = packets.to_device()?;\n        // SAFETY:\n        // - `mu_powers` has length `total_width`.\n        // - `f_ple_evals` has capacity `height * D_EF` (stacked height in base coordinates).\n        // - `d_packets` contain valid pointers and stacked row indices by construction.\n        unsafe {\n            whir_algebraic_batch_traces(&mut f_ple_evals, &d_packets, &d_mu_powers, 1 << l_skip)\n                .map_err(WhirProverError::AlgebraicBatch)?;\n        }\n        for stacked in &mut stacked_per_commit {\n            // drop traces to free device memory if RS codewords matrix exists\n            if stacked.inner.tree.backing_matrix.is_some() {\n                stacked.traces.clear();\n            }\n        }\n    } // common_main_pcs_data.matrix has now been freed\n\n    // Compute \\hat{f} coefficients:\n    //\n    // Step 1: iDFT per chunk of size 2^l_skip. After this, each chunk holds univariate\n    // coefficients c_z(x) of f(Z, x) for a fixed boolean assignment x in H_{m - l_skip}.\n    unsafe {\n        let num_poly = f_ple_evals.len() >> l_skip;\n        batch_ntt_small(&mut f_ple_evals, l_skip, num_poly, true)\n            .map_err(WhirProverError::CustomBatchIntt)?;\n    }\n    let mut f_coeffs = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(height);\n    // SAFETY: `f_ple_evals` is constructed with length `height * D_EF`.\n    unsafe {\n        transpose_fp_to_fpext_vec(&mut f_coeffs, &f_ple_evals)\n            .map_err(WhirProverError::Transpose)?;\n    }\n    drop(f_ple_evals);\n    // Step 2: Within-chunk zeta (stages 0..l_skip). Applies the subset-zeta transform\n    // over the Z-index bits, converting univariate coefficients (root-of-unity basis)\n    // into hypercube evaluations over H_{l_skip}. Together with step 1, this computes\n    // eval_to_coeff_rs_message, i.e. the MLE coefficient table of \\hat{f}.\n    for i in 0..l_skip {\n        let step = 1u32 << i;\n        // SAFETY: `f_coeffs` has length `2^m` with `m >= l_skip`.\n        unsafe {\n            mle_interpolate_stage_ext(&mut f_coeffs, step, false)\n                .map_err(|error| WhirProverError::MleInterpolate { error, step })?;\n        }\n    }\n\n    debug_assert_eq!((m - log_final_poly_len) % k_whir, 0);\n    let num_whir_rounds = (m - log_final_poly_len) / k_whir;\n    assert!(num_whir_rounds > 0);\n\n    // We maintain moments of \\hat{w}:\n    // M[T] = sum_{x superset T} \\hat{w}(x).\n    // For initial \\hat{w} = mobius_eq(u, -), these moments are exactly eq(u, -).\n    let mut w_moments = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(1 << m);\n    unsafe {\n        evals_eq_hypercube(&mut w_moments, u).map_err(WhirProverError::EvalEq)?;\n    }\n\n    let mut whir_sumcheck_polys: Vec<[EF; 2]> = vec![];\n    let mut codeword_commits = vec![];\n    let mut ood_values = vec![];\n    // per commitment, per whir query, per column\n    let mut initial_round_opened_rows: Vec<Vec<Vec<Vec<F>>>> = vec![vec![]; num_commits];\n    let mut initial_round_merkle_proofs: Vec<Vec<MerkleProof<HS::Digest>>> = vec![];\n    let mut codeword_opened_values: Vec<Vec<Vec<EF>>> = vec![];\n    let mut codeword_merkle_proofs: Vec<Vec<MerkleProof<HS::Digest>>> = vec![];\n    let mut folding_pow_witnesses = vec![];\n    let mut query_phase_pow_witnesses = vec![];\n    let mut rs_tree = None;\n    let mut log_rs_domain_size = m + log_blowup;\n    let mut final_poly = None;\n\n    let mut d_s_evals = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(2);\n    let mut d_sumcheck_tmp = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::new();\n\n    mem.tracing_info(\"before_whir_rounds\");\n    // We will drop `stacked_per_commit` and hence `common_main_pcs_data` after whir round 0.\n    for (whir_round, round_params) in whir_params.rounds.iter().enumerate() {\n        let is_last_round = whir_round == num_whir_rounds - 1;\n        // Run k_whir rounds of sumcheck on `sum_{x in H_m} \\hat{w}(\\hat{f}(x), x)`\n        for round in 0..k_whir {\n            // Do not use f_coeffs.len() because it might have extra capacity.\n            let f_height = 1 << (m - round);\n            debug_assert!(\n                f_coeffs.len() >= f_height,\n                \"f_coeffs has length {}, expected 2^{} for m={m}, round={round}\",\n                f_coeffs.len(),\n                m - round\n            );\n            debug_assert!(w_moments.len() >= f_height);\n            let output_height = f_height / 2;\n            let tmp_buffer_capacity =\n                unsafe { _whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_required_temp_buffer_size(f_height as u32) };\n            if d_sumcheck_tmp.len() < tmp_buffer_capacity as usize {\n                d_sumcheck_tmp = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(tmp_buffer_capacity as usize);\n            }\n            let mut new_f_coeffs = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(output_height);\n            let mut new_w_moments = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(output_height);\n            // SAFETY:\n            // - `d_s_evals` has length 2\n            // - `d_sumcheck_tmp` has at least required scratch length\n            unsafe {\n                whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_round(\n                    &f_coeffs,\n                    &w_moments,\n                    &mut d_s_evals,\n                    &mut d_sumcheck_tmp,\n                    f_height as u32,\n                )\n                .map_err(|error| WhirProverError::SumcheckMleRound {\n                    error,\n                    whir_round,\n                    round,\n                })?;\n            }\n            let s_evals = d_s_evals.to_host()?;\n            for &eval in &s_evals {\n                transcript.observe_ext(eval);\n            }\n            whir_sumcheck_polys.push(s_evals.try_into().unwrap());\n\n            folding_pow_witnesses.push(\n                transcript\n                    .grind_gpu(whir_params.folding_pow_bits)\n                    .map_err(WhirProverError::FoldingGrind)?,\n            );\n            let alpha = transcript.sample_ext();\n\n            // Fold `f` and `w` in coefficient/moment form with respect to `alpha`.\n            // SAFETY:\n            // - input buffers have length `f_height`.\n            // - output buffers have length `f_height / 2`.\n            unsafe {\n                whir_fold_coeffs_and_moments(\n                    &f_coeffs,\n                    &w_moments,\n                    &mut new_f_coeffs,\n                    &mut new_w_moments,\n                    alpha,\n                    f_height as u32,\n                )\n                .map_err(|error| WhirProverError::FoldMle {\n                    error,\n                    whir_round,\n                    round,\n                })?;\n            }\n            f_coeffs = new_f_coeffs;\n            w_moments = new_w_moments;\n        }\n        // Define g^ = f^(alpha, \\cdot) and send matrix commit of RS(g^)\n        // `f_coeffs` is the coefficient form of f^(alpha, \\cdot).\n        let f_height = 1 << (m - k_whir);\n        debug_assert!(f_coeffs.len() >= f_height);\n        debug_assert_eq!(size_of::<EF>() / size_of::<F>(), D_EF);\n        let mut g_coeffs = DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(f_height * D_EF);\n        // SAFETY: we allocated `f_coeffs.len() * D_EF` space for `g_coeffs` to do a 1-to-D_EF\n        // (1-to-4) split\n        unsafe {\n            split_ext_to_base_col_major_matrix(\n                &mut g_coeffs,\n                &f_coeffs,\n                f_height as u64,\n                f_height as u32,\n            )\n            .map_err(|error| WhirProverError::SplitExtPoly { error, whir_round })?;\n        }\n        let (g_tree, z_0) = if !is_last_round {\n            let codeword_height = 1 << (log_rs_domain_size - 1);\n            // `g: \\mathcal{L}^{(2)} \\to \\mathbb F`\n            let g_rs = DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(D_EF * codeword_height);\n            // SAFETY:\n            // - g_coeffs is a single EF polynomial, treated as 4 F-polynomials of height\n            //   2^{m-k_whir}\n            // - We resize each F-poly to RS domain size 2^{log_rs_domain_size - 1}, which is\n            //   equivalent to resizing the EF-polynomial\n            unsafe {\n                batch_expand_pad(\n                    g_rs.as_mut_ptr(),\n                    g_coeffs.as_ptr(),\n                    D_EF as u32,\n                    codeword_height as u32,\n                    f_height as u32,\n                )\n                .map_err(|error| WhirProverError::BatchExpandPad { error, whir_round })?;\n\n                batch_ntt(\n                    &g_rs,\n                    (log_rs_domain_size - 1) as u32,\n                    0u32,\n                    D_EF as u32,\n                    true,\n                    false,\n                );\n            }\n\n            let g_tree = MerkleTreeGpu::<F, HS::Digest>::new_with_hash::<HS::MerkleHash>(\n                DeviceMatrix::new(Arc::new(g_rs), codeword_height, D_EF),\n                1 << k_whir,\n                true,\n            )\n            .map_err(WhirProverError::MerkleTree)?;\n            let g_commit = g_tree.root();\n            transcript.observe_commit(g_commit);\n            codeword_commits.push(g_commit);\n\n            let z_0 = transcript.sample_ext();\n            // SAFETY:\n            // - `g_coeffs` is coefficient form of `\\hat{g}`, which is degree `2^{m-k_whir}`.\n            // - `g_coeffs` is F-column major matrix.\n            let g_opened_value = unsafe {\n                eval_poly_ext_at_point_from_base(&g_coeffs, 1 << (m - k_whir), z_0)\n                    .map_err(|error| WhirProverError::EvalPolyAtPoint { error, whir_round })?\n            };\n            transcript.observe_ext(g_opened_value);\n            ood_values.push(g_opened_value);\n\n            (Some(g_tree), Some(z_0))\n        } else {\n            // Observe the final poly\n            debug_assert_eq!(log_final_poly_len, m - k_whir);\n            let final_poly_len = 1 << log_final_poly_len;\n            let base_coeffs = g_coeffs.to_host()?;\n            debug_assert_eq!(base_coeffs.len(), D_EF * final_poly_len);\n            let mut coeffs = Vec::with_capacity(final_poly_len);\n            for i in 0..final_poly_len {\n                let coeff = EF::from_basis_coefficients_fn(|j| base_coeffs[j * final_poly_len + i]);\n                transcript.observe_ext(coeff);\n                coeffs.push(coeff);\n            }\n            final_poly = Some(coeffs);\n            (None, None)\n        };\n\n        // omega is generator of RS domain `\\mathcal{L}^{(2^k)}`\n        let omega = F::two_adic_generator(log_rs_domain_size - k_whir);\n        let num_queries = round_params.num_queries;\n        let mut query_indices = Vec::with_capacity(num_queries);\n        query_phase_pow_witnesses.push(\n            transcript\n                .grind_gpu(whir_params.query_phase_pow_bits)\n                .map_err(WhirProverError::QueryPhaseGrind)?,\n        );\n        // Sample query indices first\n        for _ in 0..num_queries {\n            // This is the index of the leaf in the Merkle tree\n            let index = transcript.sample_bits(log_rs_domain_size - k_whir);\n            query_indices.push(index as usize);\n        }\n        if !is_last_round {\n            codeword_opened_values.push(vec![]);\n            codeword_merkle_proofs.push(vec![]);\n        }\n        if whir_round == 0 {\n            // Vector to hold owned copies of backing matrices that are regenerated in the case they\n            // were not cached\n            let mut backing_mats_owned = vec![None; stacked_per_commit.len()];\n            let mut backing_matrices = Vec::with_capacity(stacked_per_commit.len());\n            let mut trees = Vec::with_capacity(stacked_per_commit.len());\n            for (d, backing_mat_owned) in zip(&mut stacked_per_commit, &mut backing_mats_owned) {\n                trees.push(&d.inner.tree);\n                if let Some(matrix) = d.inner.tree.backing_matrix.as_ref() {\n                    backing_matrices.push(matrix);\n                } else {\n                    let layout = d.layout();\n                    let traces = d.traces.iter().collect_vec();\n                    debug_assert!(!traces.is_empty());\n                    let backing_matrix =\n                        rs_code_matrix(log_blowup, layout, &traces, &d.inner.matrix)\n                            .map_err(WhirProverError::RsCodeMatrix)?;\n                    d.traces.clear();\n                    *backing_mat_owned = Some(backing_matrix);\n                    backing_matrices.push(backing_mat_owned.as_ref().unwrap());\n                }\n            }\n            // Get merkle proofs for in-domain samples necessary to evaluate Fold(f, \\vec\n            // \\alpha)(z_i)\n            initial_round_merkle_proofs =\n                <MerkleTreeGpu<F, HS::Digest>>::batch_query_merkle_proofs(\n                    trees.as_slice(),\n                    &query_indices,\n                )\n                .map_err(WhirProverError::MerkleTree)?;\n\n            let query_stride = trees[0].query_stride();\n            debug_assert!(\n                trees.iter().all(|tree| tree.query_stride() == query_stride),\n                \"Merkle trees don't have same layer size\"\n            );\n            let num_rows_per_query = trees[0].rows_per_query;\n            debug_assert!(\n                trees\n                    .iter()\n                    .all(|tree| tree.rows_per_query == num_rows_per_query),\n                \"Merkle trees don't have same rows_per_query\"\n            );\n\n            initial_round_opened_rows = MerkleTreeGpu::<F, HS::Digest>::batch_open_rows(\n                &backing_matrices,\n                &query_indices,\n                query_stride,\n                num_rows_per_query,\n            )\n            .map_err(WhirProverError::MerkleTree)?\n            .into_iter()\n            .map(|rows_per_commit| {\n                rows_per_commit\n                    .into_iter()\n                    .map(|rows| {\n                        let width = rows.len() / num_rows_per_query;\n                        rows.chunks_exact(width).map(|row| row.to_vec()).collect()\n                    })\n                    .collect()\n            })\n            .collect();\n            debug_assert_eq!(\n                Arc::strong_count(&stacked_per_commit[0].inner),\n                1,\n                \"common_main_pcs_data should be owned\"\n            );\n            stacked_per_commit.clear(); // this drops common_main_pcs_data\n            mem.tracing_info(\"after_initial_whir_round\");\n        } else {\n            let tree: &MerkleTreeGpu<F, HS::Digest> = rs_tree.as_ref().unwrap();\n            codeword_merkle_proofs[whir_round - 1] =\n                <MerkleTreeGpu<F, HS::Digest>>::batch_query_merkle_proofs(&[tree], &query_indices)\n                    .map_err(WhirProverError::MerkleTree)?\n                    .pop()\n                    .expect(\"exactly 1 tree\");\n            codeword_opened_values[whir_round - 1] =\n                MerkleTreeGpu::<F, HS::Digest>::batch_open_rows(\n                    &[tree.backing_matrix.as_ref().unwrap()],\n                    &query_indices,\n                    tree.query_stride(),\n                    tree.rows_per_query,\n                )\n                .map_err(WhirProverError::MerkleTree)?\n                .pop()\n                .unwrap()\n                .into_iter()\n                .map(EF::reconstitute_from_base)\n                .collect();\n        }\n        rs_tree = g_tree;\n\n        // We still sample on the last round to match the verifier, who uses a\n        // final gamma to unify some logic. But we do not need to update\n        // `w_moments`.\n        let gamma = transcript.sample_ext();\n\n        if !is_last_round {\n            // Update moments of \\hat{w}:\n            // M(T) += gamma * z0^T + sum_i gamma^{i+1} * z_i^T.\n            let log_height = (m - k_whir) as u32;\n            let z0 = z_0.unwrap();\n            let z_points = query_indices\n                .iter()\n                .map(|&index| omega.exp_u64(index as u64))\n                .collect_vec();\n\n            let mut z0_pows2 = Vec::with_capacity(log_height as usize);\n            let mut z0_pow = z0;\n            for _ in 0..log_height {\n                z0_pows2.push(z0_pow);\n                z0_pow = z0_pow.square();\n            }\n\n            let mut z_pows2 = Vec::with_capacity(num_queries * log_height as usize);\n            for z in &z_points {\n                let mut z_pow = *z;\n                for _ in 0..log_height {\n                    z_pows2.push(z_pow);\n                    z_pow = z_pow.square();\n                }\n            }\n\n            let d_z0_pows2 = z0_pows2.to_device()?;\n            let d_z_pows2 = z_pows2.to_device()?;\n            unsafe {\n                w_moments_accumulate(\n                    &mut w_moments,\n                    &d_z0_pows2,\n                    &d_z_pows2,\n                    gamma,\n                    num_queries as u32,\n                    log_height,\n                )\n                .map_err(|error| WhirProverError::WMomentsAccumulate { error, whir_round })?;\n            }\n        }\n\n        m -= k_whir;\n        log_rs_domain_size -= 1;\n    }\n\n    mem.emit_metrics();\n    Ok(WhirProof {\n        mu_pow_witness,\n        whir_sumcheck_polys,\n        codeword_commits,\n        ood_values,\n        folding_pow_witnesses,\n        query_phase_pow_witnesses,\n        initial_round_opened_rows,\n        initial_round_merkle_proofs,\n        codeword_opened_values,\n        codeword_merkle_proofs,\n        final_poly: final_poly.unwrap(),\n    })\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use std::sync::Arc;\n\n    use itertools::Itertools;\n    use openvm_stark_backend::{\n        keygen::types::MultiStarkProvingKey,\n        prover::{\n            stacked_pcs::stacked_commit, CpuColMajorBackend, DeviceDataTransporter, ProvingContext,\n        },\n        test_utils::{FibFixture, TestFixture},\n        verifier::whir::{verify_whir, VerifyWhirError},\n        StarkEngine, StarkProtocolConfig, SystemParams, WhirConfig, WhirParams,\n        WhirProximityStrategy,\n    };\n    use openvm_stark_sdk::{\n        config::{\n            baby_bear_poseidon2::{\n                default_duplex_sponge, BabyBearPoseidon2RefEngine, DuplexSponge,\n            },\n            log_up_params::log_up_security_params_baby_bear_100_bits,\n        },\n        utils::setup_tracing_with_log_level,\n    };\n    use rand::{rngs::StdRng, SeedableRng};\n    use test_case::test_case;\n    use tracing::Level;\n\n    use crate::{\n        prelude::SC, sponge::DuplexSpongeGpu, stacked_reduction::StackedPcsData2,\n        whir::prove_whir_opening_gpu, BabyBearPoseidon2GpuEngine, GpuBackend,\n    };\n\n    /// GPU-specific WHIR test runner. Uses `prove_whir_opening_gpu` for the\n    /// proving step and the shared CPU verifier for verification.\n    fn run_whir_test_gpu(\n        params: SystemParams,\n        pk: MultiStarkProvingKey<SC>,\n        ctx: ProvingContext<CpuColMajorBackend<SC>>,\n    ) -> Result<(), VerifyWhirError> {\n        let engine = BabyBearPoseidon2GpuEngine::new(params.clone());\n        let device = engine.device();\n        let mut rng = StdRng::seed_from_u64(0);\n        let (z_prism, z_cube) = openvm_backend_tests::generate_random_z(&params, &mut rng);\n\n        let common_main_traces = ctx\n            .common_main_traces()\n            .map(|(_, trace)| trace)\n            .collect_vec();\n        // Use CPU stacked_commit to isolate GPU testing to WHIR prover\n        let (common_main_commit, common_main_pcs_data) = stacked_commit(\n            engine.config().hasher(),\n            params.l_skip,\n            params.n_stack,\n            params.log_blowup,\n            params.k_whir(),\n            &common_main_traces,\n        )\n        .unwrap();\n        let d_common_main_traces = common_main_traces\n            .iter()\n            .map(|t| {\n                <_ as DeviceDataTransporter<SC, GpuBackend>>::transport_matrix_to_device(device, t)\n            })\n            .collect_vec();\n        let d_common_main_pcs_data =\n            <_ as DeviceDataTransporter<SC, GpuBackend>>::transport_pcs_data_to_device(\n                device,\n                &common_main_pcs_data,\n            );\n\n        let mut stacking_openings = vec![openvm_backend_tests::stacking_openings_for_matrix(\n            &params,\n            &z_prism,\n            &common_main_pcs_data.matrix,\n        )];\n        let mut commits = vec![common_main_commit];\n        let mut stacked_per_commit = vec![StackedPcsData2 {\n            inner: Arc::new(d_common_main_pcs_data),\n            traces: d_common_main_traces,\n        }];\n        for (air_id, air_ctx) in ctx.per_trace {\n            for data in pk.per_air[air_id]\n                .preprocessed_data\n                .iter()\n                .chain(air_ctx.cached_mains.iter().map(|cd| &cd.data))\n            {\n                let trace =\n                    <_ as DeviceDataTransporter<SC, GpuBackend>>::transport_matrix_to_device(\n                        device,\n                        &data.mat_view(0).to_matrix(),\n                    );\n                commits.push(data.commit().unwrap());\n                stacking_openings.push(openvm_backend_tests::stacking_openings_for_matrix(\n                    &params,\n                    &z_prism,\n                    &data.matrix,\n                ));\n                let d_data =\n                    <_ as DeviceDataTransporter<SC, GpuBackend>>::transport_pcs_data_to_device(\n                        device, data,\n                    );\n                stacked_per_commit.push(StackedPcsData2 {\n                    inner: Arc::new(d_data),\n                    traces: vec![trace],\n                });\n            }\n        }\n\n        let mut prover_sponge = DuplexSpongeGpu::default();\n\n        let proof = prove_whir_opening_gpu::<crate::DefaultHashScheme, _>(\n            &params,\n            &mut prover_sponge,\n            stacked_per_commit,\n            &z_cube,\n        )\n        .unwrap();\n\n        let mut verifier_sponge = default_duplex_sponge();\n        verify_whir(\n            &mut verifier_sponge,\n            engine.config(),\n            &proof,\n            &stacking_openings,\n            &commits,\n            &z_cube,\n        )\n    }\n\n    fn run_whir_fib_test_gpu(params: SystemParams) -> Result<(), VerifyWhirError> {\n        let engine = BabyBearPoseidon2RefEngine::<DuplexSponge>::new(params.clone());\n        let fib = FibFixture::new(0, 1, 1 << params.log_stacked_height());\n        let (pk, _vk) = fib.keygen(&engine);\n        let ctx = fib.generate_proving_ctx();\n        run_whir_test_gpu(params, pk, ctx)\n    }\n\n    fn whir_test_params(k_whir: usize, log_final_poly_len: usize) -> WhirParams {\n        WhirParams {\n            k: k_whir,\n            log_final_poly_len,\n            query_phase_pow_bits: 2,\n            folding_pow_bits: 1,\n            mu_pow_bits: 3,\n            proximity: WhirProximityStrategy::UniqueDecoding,\n        }\n    }\n\n    #[test_case(0, 1, 1, 0)]\n    #[test_case(2, 1, 1, 2)]\n    #[test_case(2, 1, 2, 0)]\n    #[test_case(2, 1, 3, 1)]\n    #[test_case(2, 1, 4, 0)]\n    #[test_case(2, 2, 4, 0)]\n    fn test_whir_single_fib_gpu(\n        n_stack: usize,\n        log_blowup: usize,\n        k_whir: usize,\n        log_final_poly_len: usize,\n    ) -> Result<(), VerifyWhirError> {\n        setup_tracing_with_log_level(Level::DEBUG);\n\n        let l_skip = 2;\n        let w_stack = 8;\n        let whir = WhirConfig::new(\n            log_blowup,\n            l_skip + n_stack,\n            whir_test_params(k_whir, log_final_poly_len),\n            10,\n        );\n        let params = SystemParams {\n            l_skip: 2,\n            n_stack,\n            w_stack,\n            log_blowup,\n            whir,\n            logup: log_up_security_params_baby_bear_100_bits(),\n            max_constraint_degree: 3,\n        };\n        run_whir_fib_test_gpu(params)\n    }\n\n    // TODO: test multiple commitments with GPU prover\n}\n","numLines":718,"startLine":1,"totalLines":718}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SBe92pnkxVa7ij5eAtuunf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good understanding of the WHIR prover. Let me think about optimization opportunities.\n\nThe WHIR prover flow:\n1. Algebraic batching: `whir_algebraic_batch_traces` — batches all traces into one polynomial (18ms kernel)\n2. Coefficient computation: batch_ntt_small (iDFT) + transpose + mle_interpolate_stages\n3. For each WHIR round (num_whir_rounds iterations):\n   a. k_whir inner sumcheck rounds: `whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_round` + D2H + transcript + `whir_fold_coeffs_and_moments`\n   b. Split extension field to base, then batch expand and pad with RS encoding of the folded polynomial\n   c. Commit via Merkle tree on GPU\n   d. Update transcript and sample challenges\n   e. Evaluate the polynomial at out-of-domain points\n   f. Query and open Merkle proofs for the required rows\n   g. Accumulate moment updates\n\nThe WHIR round is fundamentally sequential, with the Merkle tree commitment and polynomial evaluation being the most computationally intensive steps per round.\n\nSince data shrinks by half each round, the first round is the bottleneck. Looking at the nsight profiling data, I can see the specific kernel breakdown—the algebraic batching kernel takes about 18ms across 6 instances, while the fold and moments kernel runs at 3.3ms across 80 instances. This tells me where the actual GPU time is being spent and what might be worth optimizing further. Looking at the per-segment breakdown, Merkle tree commitments and grinding appear to be the dominant costs at around 15-20ms and 6ms respectively, with CPU overhead and transcript handling adding another 20ms — so optimizing the grinding step could yield meaningful improvements.\n\nChecking the `grind_kernel` profiling data, I see 207 instances totaling 18ms, which comes from multiple PoW challenges per WHIR round across the folding, query, and mu phases. While 18ms isn't massive, there's likely room to optimize the GPU thread utilization here.\n\nNow I need to figure out where to focus for meaningful gains. The STARK excluding trace is at 1137ms and needs to drop to around 898ms—that's a 21% reduction. Round 0 and MLE Rounds are already hitting their per-AIR limits, and LogUp GKR is kernel-bound, so the real opportunities are in Trace Commit at 196ms, WHIR at 129ms, or finding ways to overlap work across phases.\n\nLooking at the phase dependencies more closely: Constraints produces the opening point `r` that Openings needs, so they can't run in parallel. But within Openings itself, there might be room to start Stacked Reduction before Constraints fully completes—I need to check if `u_prisma` and `stacked_per_commit` could be computed earlier or if there's any dependency I'm missing.\n\nActually, examining the code flow, Stacked Reduction requires `r` from the start, so that won't work. But I'm noticing something else: the Merkle tree intermediate layers built during Trace Commit aren't actually needed until WHIR does query openings later. So instead of computing all those layers upfront, I could just compute the root during Trace Commit and rebuild the tree layers on-demand during WHIR—this would save roughly 12ms in the Trace Commit phase.\n\nThat's probably not worth the added complexity though. Let me consider a different angle: what if I overlap the NTT computation of the RS code matrix with the Merkle tree hashing using separate GPU streams? The issue is that the hashing depends on the NTT output, so they can't truly run in parallel. But what if I process the codeword matrix column-by-column, hashing each column as soon as the NTT finishes producing it?\n\nThe problem is that the Merkle tree hashes entire rows, which span all columns, so I'd need every column ready before I could hash even a single row. Restructuring the hash to work column-by-column would change the protocol entirely.\n\nI think I need to step back and focus on concrete improvements to the current implementation. Let me examine the row hashing kernel more closely...\n\nExamining the row hashing kernel...\n\nThe kernel iterates through all columns for each row, feeding them into Poseidon2 in chunks of 8 elements. At 106K columns with a rate of 8, that's roughly 13K mix operations per thread. The memory access pattern reads from different columns with a stride of `height` between them, which means adjacent threads within a warp access adjacent rows in the same column—that part is coalesced. But the column loop itself has poor...\n\nThe stride between consecutive column reads is massive—at height ~262K and 4 bytes per element, that's 1MB between reads, far beyond what the L2 cache can handle. So while individual reads are coalesced, the kernel is fundamentally memory-bandwidth-bound, pulling small chunks from scattered memory regions. Changing the matrix to row-major layout would fix this, but that would ripple through the entire codebase since column-major is used everywhere for NTT and constraints. An alternative would be to copy the matrix to row-major format just before building the Merkle tree, so each thread reads consecutive elements sequentially.\n\nBut I need to check if this transpose is actually feasible. The cost would be transposing the full matrix—at APC 300 with 811M cells across 106K columns, that's roughly 7600 rows per column, not the 262K I initially thought. Let me recalculate what the actual matrix dimensions are based on the stacking parameters.\n\nWith stacking, the height becomes a power of 2. So if I have 405M cells per segment and 106K columns, the height works out to around 4096 after rounding up. After RS expansion doubles it to 8192, transposing that 8192 × 106K matrix would cost about 3.3 GB of data movement—roughly 3.3 milliseconds on a GPU with 1 TB/s bandwidth. Whether this is worth it depends on how much the hash kernel benefits from better memory locality.\n\nThe real tradeoff is between row-major access (where a warp reads 13.6MB sequentially) versus column-major access (where stride-8192 jumps cause TLB misses and scattered memory pages). Even though row-major has better locality, both patterns are bandwidth-bound since 13.6MB exceeds the cache. The question is whether column-major strides degrade DRAM throughput enough on modern GPUs to justify the transpose overhead.\n\nActually, I'm realizing the current kernel already coalesces threads within a warp—they access consecutive rows in the same column. When warps advance through columns, the memory controller can batch requests efficiently since all warps are reading from the same column simultaneously. This is a standard GPU matrix traversal pattern and should achieve good bandwidth utilization.\n\nSo the Merkle tree hashing is likely already near bandwidth-optimal. The only real improvements would require changing the protocol itself—either reducing the data volume or using a faster hash function. Let me think about what else could actually be optimized.\n\nAfter 45 iterations of tuning, the system has hit its limits. The bottlenecks are components that don't scale with APC count due to fundamental per-AIR overhead, sequential phases that can't be parallelized, and bandwidth-bound operations like Merkle trees and NTTs. I'm wondering if there's a different angle—what if we reduced the number of segments at APC 0? But wait, we're optimizing for APC 300, not APC 0, and the segment count is determined by the guest program anyway. The actual goal is getting APC 300 STARK time below half of APC 0's time, and we're currently at 1137ms versus 1795ms.\n\nNow I'm looking at what the theoretical minimum could be given the hardware constraints. The GKR inner rounds are kernel-bound at around 120ms per segment, input evaluation takes 66ms per segment, Round 0 runs at 93ms per segment on 8 threads, and MLE rounds are at 80ms per segment. Since these phases run sequentially