... })`\n- Memory: Pre-allocates buffers based on max AIR height and interaction count\n- Barrier sync after GPU work (line 282: `current_stream_sync()`) ensures visibility\n- Outputs: `DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` leaves + `alpha_logup` scalar\n- Line 488: Memory metrics emitted\n\n---\n\n### PHASE 1: GKR Inner Rounds (Lines 490-498)\n**Function:** `fractional_sumcheck_gpu()` in `fractional.rs` (Line 491)\n\n**What it does:**\n- Executes l_skip + n_logup rounds of GKR sumcheck protocol on the interaction tree\n- Builds segment tree bottom-up from leaves\n- Fuses multiple rounds into single kernel passes for efficiency\n- Uses bitrev + tree layers 0+1 fused kernel for large N (>1024)\n- Returns final xi challenges and GKR proof\n\n**Key Details:**\n- **No thread::scope here** - runs single-threaded on CUDA device\n- Each round computes line polynomial and evaluates at random challenge\n- Fuses consecutive pairs of tree layers (lines 559-575)\n- Line 576: Memory metrics emitted after tree construction\n- **Memory: Reuses single layer buffer throughout** to minimize peak usage\n- Outputs: `xi` vector (concatenates to l_skip + n_global challenges), `FracSumcheckProof`\n\n---\n\n### PHASE 2: Round 0 Evaluation (Lines 510-620)\n**Two sub-phases with concurrent execution:**\n\n#### Phase 2A: Round 0 GPU Constraint Evaluation (Lines 510-620)\n**Function:** `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()` in `mod.rs` (Line 948)\n\n**What it does:**\n- Evaluates plain AIR constraints and interaction constraints on the hypercube at cosets\n- Performs polynomial extraction (transpose + iDFT + Lagrange interpolation)\n- **Concurrent execution:** Main thread (Round 0 evals) + Background thread (eq_3b upload + logup combinations precompute)\n\n**Key Details:**\n- Line 1367: **`std::thread::scope` with dual workers:**\n  - **Background thread (lines 1371-1407):** Uploads `eq_3b_per_trace` to device + precomputes `logup_combinations`\n  - **Main threads (lines 1410-1432):** Multiple worker threads process