{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wpnn7rSdVU22hpbihTKoLt","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4e113b8-a396-45cc-8e86-654a475f0e59","uuid":"65ee2dc7-cd1b-43d4-83fe-34cc045da374","timestamp":"2026-04-16T13:13:42.142Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-16-1300-tune-merkle-hash-grid-for-small-query-stride\n\nReduce the GPU SM underutilization in `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel` when `query_stride` is small (APC 300: 1024 rows) by launching more, smaller thread blocks. Currently the launcher uses `blockDim.x = 512 >> log_rows_per_query = 32`, producing only 32 blocks for `query_stride = 1024` — occupying 32 of 128 SMs (25%). Reducing `blockDim.x` to 4-8 increases the block count to 128-256, achieving full SM utilization and an estimated 2-3x speedup on the compute-bound row hashing kernel. This specifically improves APC 300 Trace Commit (where the stacked matrix is wide but short) without affecting APC 0 (which already has full SM utilization from its taller matrix).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1,"newLines":3,"lines":["-# 2026-04-16-1100-tune-gkr-precompute-m-parameters","+# 2026-04-16-1300-tune-merkle-hash-grid-for-small-query-stride"," ","-Tune the GKR fractional sumcheck PrecomputeM strategy parameters (`TARGET_BLOCKS`, `MIN_BLOCKS`, `MIN_N`, `TAIL_TILE`) to reduce the GKR inner round cost at APC 300. The GKR inner rounds are the single largest sequential component at 213ms (107ms per segment), with `precompute_m_build_partial` at 45ms and `multifold` at 47ms being the dominant kernels. The current defaults (`TARGET_BLOCKS=1024`, `MIN_BLOCKS=64`, `MIN_N=22`, `TAIL_TILE=4096`) were set without specific tuning for the APC 300 workload, which has a different GKR tree shape (more traces, smaller per-trace) than APC 0. Parameter sweeping via the existing `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_*` environment variables can identify a configuration that better balances GPU parallelism and per-window overhead for this workload.","+Reduce the GPU SM underutilization in `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel` when `query_stride` is small (APC 300: 1024 rows) by launching more, smaller thread blocks. Currently the launcher uses `blockDim.x = 512 >> log_rows_per_query = 32`, producing only 32 blocks for `query_stride = 1024` — occupying 32 of 128 SMs (25%). Reducing `blockDim.x` to 4-8 increases the block count to 128-256, achieving full SM utilization and an estimated 2-3x speedup on the compute-bound row hashing kernel. This specifically improves APC 300 Trace Commit (where the stacked matrix is wide but short) without affecting APC 0 (which already has full SM utilization from its taller matrix)."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-16-1100-tune-gkr-precompute-m-parameters\n\nTune the GKR fractional sumcheck PrecomputeM strategy parameters (`TARGET_BLOCKS`, `MIN_BLOCKS`, `MIN_N`, `TAIL_TILE`) to reduce the GKR inner round cost at APC 300. The GKR inner rounds are the single largest sequential component at 213ms (107ms per segment), with `precompute_m_build_partial` at 45ms and `multifold` at 47ms being the dominant kernels. The current defaults (`TARGET_BLOCKS=1024`, `MIN_BLOCKS=64`, `MIN_N=22`, `TAIL_TILE=4096`) were set without specific tuning for the APC 300 workload, which has a different GKR tree shape (more traces, smaller per-trace) than APC 0. Parameter sweeping via the existing `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_*` environment variables can identify a configuration that better balances GPU parallelism and per-window overhead for this workload.\n"}}
