{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018HnWtUM1CmqxKvvSAFpAUU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Tune Merkle Hash Grid for Small Query Stride\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tIncrease GPU SM utilization for the `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel` when the Merkle tree has a small `query_stride` (≤ 4096). At APC 300, the stacked codeword matrix is wide (~53K columns per segment) but short (query_stride ≈ 1024), producing only 32 thread blocks — occupying 32 of 128 SMs (25%). Reducing `blockDim.x` increases the block count to 128+, achieving near-full SM utilization and an estimated 2-3x speedup on this compute-bound kernel. This specifically improves APC 300 Trace Commit without affecting APC 0 (which already has 2048+ blocks).\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### Launcher\n10\t\n11\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/merkle_tree.cu`, lines 214-231\n12\t\n13\t```cpp\n14\textern \"C\" int _poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes(\n15\t    digest_t *out,\n16\t    const Fp *matrix,\n17\t    size_t width,\n18\t    size_t query_stride,\n19\t    size_t log_rows_per_query\n20\t) {\n21\t    auto [grid, block] = kernel_launch_params(query_stride, 512 >> log_rows_per_query);\n22\t    block.y = 1 << log_rows_per_query;\n23\t    size_t shared_stride = block.x * div_ceil(block.y, 2);\n24\t    size_t shmem_bytes = CELLS_OUT * shared_stride * sizeof(Fp);\n25\t    auto height = query_stride << log_rows_per_query;\n26\t    poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel<<<grid, block, shmem_bytes>>>(...);\n27\t    return CHECK_KERNEL();\n28\t}\n29\t```\n30\t\n31\t**`kernel_launch_params`** (`crates/cuda-common/include/launcher.cuh`, line 14):\n32\t```cpp\n33\tinline std::pair<dim3, dim3> kernel_launch_params(size_t count, size_t threads_per_block) {\n34\t    size_t block = std::min(count, threads_per_block);\n35\t    size_t grid = div_ceil(count, block);\n36\t    return std::make_pair(dim3(grid, 1, 1), dim3(block, 1, 1));\n37\t}\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\t### Current launch geometry at APC 300\n41\t\n42\t- `log_rows_per_query` = `k_whir` = 4 (from `SystemParams::k_whir()`)\n43\t- `threads_per_block` = 512 >> 4 = 32\n44\t- `query_stride` ≈ 1024 (codeword_height / 2^k_whir, where codeword_height ≈ 2^14)\n45\t- `blockDim` = (32, 16) = 512 threads/block\n46\t- `gridDim` = (ceil(1024/32), 1) = (32, 1) = **32 blocks**\n47\t- SM utilization: 32 / 128 = **25%**\n48\t\n49\t### Current launch geometry at APC 0\n50\t\n51\t- Same `k_whir` = 4\n52\t- `query_stride` ≈ 65536 (codeword_height / 16, where codeword_height ≈ 2^20)\n53\t- `blockDim` = (32, 16) = 512 threads/block\n54\t- `gridDim` = (ceil(65536/32), 1) = (2048, 1) = 2048 blocks\n55\t- SM utilization: **100%** (2048 >> 128)\n56\t\n57\t### Kernel structure\n58\t\n59\tThe kernel (`merkle_tree.cu`, line 16) has two phases:\n60\t\n61\t1. **Row hashing** (lines 39-51): Each thread (indexed by `stride_idx = blockDim.x * blockIdx.x + threadIdx.x`) iterates over all `width` columns, absorbing elements into a Poseidon2 sponge (CELLS=16, CELLS_RATE=8). At APC 300 with width ≈ 53K, this is ≈ 6625 `poseidon2_mix` calls per thread.\n62\t\n63\t2. **Intra-query Merkle reduction** (lines 53-71): `log_rows_per_query` levels of tree compression in shared memory across the y-dimension. `blockDim.y = 2^log_rows_per_query = 16`. Each level halves active y-threads, combining adjacent digests via `poseidon2_mix`.\n64\t\n65\t**Key observation**: `blockDim.x` controls how many stride positions are processed per block. Reducing it increases the block count without changing the total thread count or work assignment — each thread still processes one stride position.\n66\t\n67\t### Callers\n68\t\n69\t- `stacked_commit` → `MerkleTreeGpu::new_with_hash` → `compress_rows` → `_poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes` — the main trace commitment Merkle tree, called once per segment.\n70\t- `prove_whir_opening_gpu` → `MerkleTreeGpu::new_with_hash` — WHIR round commits, which have width=4 (tiny rows, not affected by this optimization).\n71\t- There is an extension-field variant `_poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_ext` with the same launcher pattern (line 233-250), used for extension-field Merkle trees. The same fix should be applied there for consistency.\n72\t\n73\t## Changes\n74\t\n75\t### Change 1: Add adaptive blockDim.x selection in the hash launcher\n76\t\n77\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/merkle_tree.cu`, lines 214-231\n78\t\n79\tReplace the fixed `512 >> log_rows_per_query` with an adaptive choice:\n80\t\n81\t```cpp\n82\textern \"C\" int _poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes(\n83\t    digest_t *out,\n84\t    const Fp *matrix,\n85\t    size_t width,\n86\t    size_t query_stride,\n87\t    size_t log_rows_per_query\n88\t) {\n89\t    // Target: enough blocks to fill all SMs (≥128 blocks on RTX 4090).\n90\t    // Each block has blockDim.y = 2^log_rows_per_query threads for Merkle\n91\t    // levels, and blockDim.x threads for stride parallelism.\n92\t    // Default blockDim.x = 512 >> log_rows_per_query (e.g. 32 for k=4).\n93\t    // When query_stride is small, this produces too few blocks.\n94\t    // We reduce blockDim.x until grid has ≥ MIN_BLOCKS blocks.\n95\t    constexpr size_t MIN_BLOCKS = 128;\n96\t    size_t default_bx = 512 >> log_rows_per_query;\n97\t    size_t bx = default_bx;\n98\t    while (bx > 1 && div_ceil(query_stride, bx) < MIN_BLOCKS) {\n99\t        bx >>= 1;\n100\t    }\n101\t    auto [grid, block] = kernel_launch_params(query_stride, bx);\n102\t    block.y = 1 << log_rows_per_query;\n103\t    size_t shared_stride = block.x * div_ceil(block.y, 2);\n104\t    size_t shmem_bytes = CELLS_OUT * shared_stride * sizeof(Fp);\n105\t    auto height = query_stride << log_rows_per_query;\n106\t\n107\t    poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel<<<grid, block, shmem_bytes>>>(\n108\t        out, matrix, width, height, query_stride, log_rows_per_query\n109\t    );\n110\t    return CHECK_KERNEL();\n111\t}\n112\t```\n113\t\n114\t**Why this helps**: At APC 300 with query_stride=1024, the loop reduces bx from 32 → 16 → 8, giving grid.x = ceil(1024/8) = 128 blocks. This uses all 128 SMs instead of 32. The shared memory per block shrinks proportionally (from 8192 to 2048 bytes), well within limits.\n115\t\n116\t**APC 0 is unaffected**: query_stride=65536, div_ceil(65536,32) = 2048 ≥ 128, so bx stays at 32 (default path).\n117\t\n118\t### Change 2: Apply the same fix to the ext variant\n119\t\n120\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/merkle_tree.cu`, lines 233-250\n121\t\n122\tApply the identical `MIN_BLOCKS` adaptive logic to `_poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_ext`. Same loop, same constant.\n123\t\n124\t### Change 3 (optional, if needed): Adjust __syncthreads usage\n125\t\n126\tThe kernel uses `__syncthreads()` in the Merkle reduction phase (lines 61, 71). With blockDim = (8, 16) = 128 threads = 4 warps, `__syncthreads` is slightly more expensive than within a single warp. However, for correctness, `__syncthreads` is required when any pair of threads in different warps share data via shared memory. At blockDim.x = 8, two x-threads can be in different warps (if y-threads of the same warp span different x-indices). So `__syncthreads` is still required. No change needed to the kernel itself.\n127\t\n128\t## Invariants\n129\t\n130\t1. **Correctness**: The kernel output must be identical regardless of `blockDim.x`. Each thread processes exactly one stride position (`stride_idx = blockDim.x * blockIdx.x + threadIdx.x`). The Merkle reduction in shared memory operates within a block's y-dimension. Reducing blockDim.x only changes how stride positions are distributed across blocks — the per-thread computation is unchanged.\n131\t\n132\t2. **APC 0 no-regression**: When query_stride is large (≥ default_bx × MIN_BLOCKS), the adaptive loop doesn't fire and the launch geometry is identical to today.\n133\t\n134\t3. **Shared memory correctness**: `shared_stride = block.x * div_ceil(block.y, 2)`. With smaller block.x, shared_stride shrinks, but each y-layer exchange accesses `shared_offset = ((leaf_idx >> (layer+1)) << layer) * block.x + threadIdx.x`, which stays within bounds.\n135\t\n136\t4. **Thread count**: Total threads = grid.x × block.x × block.y = query_stride × (1 << log_rows_per_query) = height. This is preserved regardless of the block.x choice.\n137\t\n138\t## Measurement Plan\n139\t\n140\t1. Run `run_pairing.sh` for APC 0, 100, 300 before and after the change.\n141\t2. Compare `STARK (excl. trace)` and `Trace Commit` metrics.\n142\t3. Run nsight profile on APC 300 to verify:\n143\t   - `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel` instance count is unchanged (25)\n144\t   - Average/total kernel time decreased for the large instances (main trace commits)\n145\t   - Grid dimensions increased from 32 to 128 for main trace commits\n146\t4. APC 0 must show no regression (within ±20ms noise).\n147\t\n148\t## Rollback Criteria\n149\t\n150\t- Less than 15ms improvement on STARK excl trace at APC 300.\n151\t- Any regression > 20ms on STARK excl trace at APC 0.\n152\t- Any correctness failure (proof verification fails).\n153\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UzkbupN6iRDHaGxfyp7Mav","session_id":"b4e113b8-a396-45cc-8e86-654a475f0e59","uuid":"f16d4807-e632-428f-b792-c806114273b8","timestamp":"2026-04-16T13:15:15.639Z"}
