{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T36jpkHRjyXPmz7Mi6QgYK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-16-1300-tune-merkle-hash-grid-for-small-query-stride\n2\t\n3\tReduce the GPU SM underutilization in `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel` when `query_stride` is small (APC 300: 1024 rows) by launching more, smaller thread blocks. Currently the launcher uses `blockDim.x = 512 >> log_rows_per_query = 32`, producing only 32 blocks for `query_stride = 1024` — occupying 32 of 128 SMs (25%). Reducing `blockDim.x` to 4-8 increases the block count to 128-256, achieving full SM utilization and an estimated 2-3x speedup on the compute-bound row hashing kernel. This specifically improves APC 300 Trace Commit (where the stacked matrix is wide but short) without affecting APC 0 (which already has full SM utilization from its taller matrix).\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UzkbupN6iRDHaGxfyp7Mav","session_id":"b4e113b8-a396-45cc-8e86-654a475f0e59","uuid":"eb4db15e-d0f8-47b3-b9d6-71bada0e04b9","timestamp":"2026-04-16T13:18:13.129Z"}
