{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QA6JVkTcia47Rt6NZo7Ny3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-16-1430-column-batched-ntt-for-rs-code-matrix\n2\t\n3\tImprove the NTT memory access efficiency in `rs_code_matrix` by processing columns in L2-cache-sized batches instead of all columns simultaneously. The current `batch_ntt` processes all ~53K columns (at APC 300) in a single call, creating a 3.4GB working set that far exceeds the RTX 4090's 72MB L2 cache. This forces every NTT butterfly stage to read from DRAM at large strides, achieving only ~30% of peak bandwidth. By splitting the NTT into batches of ~1000 columns (~64MB per batch, fitting in L2), the second NTT stage reads data that's still L2-resident from the first stage, potentially doubling effective bandwidth. This improvement disproportionately helps APC 300 (short columns, 64KB each, excellent L2 reuse) over APC 0 (tall columns, 4MB each, less L2 benefit).\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01J1PSSGwTrH8SjJVxPqzM2B","session_id":"b4e113b8-a396-45cc-8e86-654a475f0e59","uuid":"6101e2f5-fb36-40c8-8b69-ea249407feba","timestamp":"2026-04-16T13:26:02.521Z"}
