{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TmCxa28LAp3bg7ajycfJ1i","type":"tool_result","content":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/report.md-3-## Description\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/report.md-4-\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/report.md:5:Move the Stacked Reduction Round 0 polynomial reconstruction (`reconstruct_s0_from_g` + `ntt_multiply_and_add`) from CPU to GPU using a multi-kernel pipeline. The current CPU-side implementation performs per-bucket D2H transfers (each syncing the stream), followed by serial iDFT, DFT, pointwise multiplication, and inverse DFT on the host. The GPU pipeline eliminates per-bucket D2H syncs and replaces CPU NTT operations with batched GPU NTT calls via `batch_ntt_small`.\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/report.md-6-\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/report.md-7-The expected improvement was ~10ms on the 75ms Stacked Reduction span (~3.6ms from eliminating D2H syncs + ~6-8ms from moving CPU NTT to GPU).\n--\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/report.md-21-\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/report.md-22-- **`crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`**: \nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/report.md:23:  - Added imports for `batch_ntt_small`, `split_ext_to_base_col_major_matrix`, `batch_expand_pad`, `transpose_fp_to_fpext_vec`, and the new kernel wrappers\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/report.md-24-  - Added `reconstruct_s0_from_g_gpu` method: Pre-computes all E evaluations on CPU, uploads once, then runs GPU pipeline per bucket\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/report.md-25-  - Added `gpu_ntt_multiply_and_accumulate` helper: 10-step GPU pipeline per bucket (AoS→SoA → iDFT → zero-pad → DFT → SoA→AoS → pointwise mul → AoS→SoA → iDFT → SoA→AoS → accumulate)\n--\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/report.md-69-- **The CPU polynomial reconstruction is not a bottleneck**: At 2-3ms of the 75ms Stacked Reduction total, it's only ~3-4% of the component and <0.3% of STARK excl trace. No further optimization of this path is worthwhile.\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/report.md-70-- **Stacked Reduction's dominant cost is the per-trace kernel loop** (`batch_sumcheck_uni_round0_poly` GPU kernels) which computes G0/G1/G2. Multi-streaming this was attempted previously and failed due to accumulation buffer issues.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/report.md:71:- **The GPU NTT pipeline infrastructure** (AoS↔SoA + batch_ntt_small) works correctly and could be reused for other small polynomial operations, but the kernel launch overhead limits applicability for sub-1000-element operations.\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/report.md-72-- **Kernel fusion** (combining multiple steps of the pipeline into a single kernel) could reduce launch overhead but adds significant complexity for minimal gain at these scales.\n--\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-3-## Goal\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-4-\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md:5:Move the Stacked Reduction Round 0 polynomial reconstruction (`reconstruct_s0_from_g` + `ntt_multiply_and_add`) from CPU to GPU using a multi-kernel pipeline with the existing `batch_ntt_small` primitive. This eliminates per-bucket D2H + stream sync overhead (~3.6ms) and moves the NTT compute to GPU (~6-10ms CPU NTT → <1ms GPU NTT), for an estimated net ~10ms improvement on the 74ms Stacked Reduction span.\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-6-\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-7-## Current Code Path\n--\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-35-### Overview: Multi-kernel GPU pipeline\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-36-\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md:37:Replace the CPU `ntt_multiply_and_add` with a GPU pipeline using existing `batch_ntt_small` and two small new CUDA kernels (AoS↔SoA transpose, pointwise multiply+sum). No fused kernel — each step is a separate kernel launch for correctness and simplicity.\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-38-\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-39-Pipeline per bucket:\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-40-1. G evaluations already on GPU (in d_g_pos / d_g_neg)\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-41-2. GPU: AoS → SoA transpose (FpExt → 4 × Fp layout)\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md:42:3. GPU: `batch_ntt_small(is_intt=true)` on Fp data — iDFT of G evals → G coefficients\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-43-4. GPU: Zero-pad G from skip_domain to large_uni_domain\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-44-5. E evaluations pre-computed and pre-uploaded (see Step 6 in orchestration)\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md:45:6. GPU: `batch_ntt_small(is_intt=false)` on Fp data — DFT of G coefficients → G evals\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-46-7. GPU: SoA→AoS of G via `transpose_fp_to_fpext_vec`\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-47-8. GPU: Pointwise EF multiply+sum kernel: s[j] = Σᵢ E_i[j] × G_i[j]\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-48-9. GPU: AoS→SoA of s via `split_ext_to_base_col_major_matrix`\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md:49:10. GPU: `batch_ntt_small(is_intt=true)` on s — iDFT → product coefficients\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-50-11. GPU: SoA→AoS of result via `transpose_fp_to_fpext_vec`\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-51-12. GPU: Accumulate into d_s0_accum (element-wise add, no atomics — same stream)\n--\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-59-- **SoA→AoS (4×Fp → EF)**: `transpose_fp_to_fpext_vec` in `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/poly.rs:56`\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-60-\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md:61:These are already used by the WHIR prover (`crates/cuda-backend/src/whir.rs:100-153`) for exactly this pattern: convert EF to Fp SoA, run `batch_ntt_small`, convert back. No new kernels needed for AoS↔SoA.\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-62-\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-63-### Step 2: Pointwise EF multiply-sum kernel\n--\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-140-1. **AoS→SoA of G**: `split_ext_to_base_col_major_matrix` on d_g_evals (3 × skip_domain EF → SoA Fp buffer with 4 × 3 × skip_domain elements)\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-141-\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md:142:2. **iDFT of G (SoA)**: `batch_ntt_small(d_g_soa, l_skip, cnt_blocks=12, is_intt=true)` — 12 = 4 components × 3 vectors, each 2^l_skip Fp elements. Output is natural-order (confirmed by existing usage in sumcheck.rs:200-234)\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-143-\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-144-3. **SoA→AoS of G coefficients**: `transpose_fp_to_fpext_vec` on d_g_soa → d_g_aos (3 × skip_domain EF)\n--\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-148-5. **AoS→SoA of padded G**: `split_ext_to_base_col_major_matrix` on d_g_padded (3 × large_uni_domain EF → SoA Fp)\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-149-\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md:150:6. **DFT of G (SoA)**: `batch_ntt_small(d_g_soa_large, l_skip+1, cnt_blocks=12, is_intt=false)`\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-151-\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-152-7. **SoA→AoS of G evals**: `transpose_fp_to_fpext_vec` on d_g_soa_large → d_g_aos_evals\n--\nautoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md-156-9. **AoS→SoA of product**: `split_ext_to_base_col_major_matrix` on d_s_work (large_uni_domain EF → SoA Fp)\n\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 60]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01J1PSSGwTrH8SjJVxPqzM2B","session_id":"b4e113b8-a396-45cc-8e86-654a475f0e59","uuid":"28