{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MuseRiHX6ftbDkrYNVbYke","type":"tool_result","content":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-16-1430-column-batched-ntt-for-rs-code-matrix\n\nImprove the NTT memory access efficiency in `rs_code_matrix` by processing columns in L2-cache-sized batches instead of all columns simultaneously. The current `batch_ntt` processes all ~53K columns (at APC 300) in a single call, creating a 3.4GB working set that far exceeds the RTX 4090's 72MB L2 cache. This forces every NTT butterfly stage to read from DRAM at large strides, achieving only ~30% of peak bandwidth. By splitting the NTT into batches of ~1000 columns (~64MB per batch, fitting in L2), the second NTT stage reads data that's still L2-resident from the first stage, potentially doubling effective bandwidth. This improvement disproportionately helps APC 300 (short columns, 64KB each, excellent L2 reuse) over APC 0 (tall columns, 4MB each, less L2 benefit).\n\n=== plan.md exists ===\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 georg georg 11389 Apr 16 15:30 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-1430-column-batched-ntt-for-rs-code-matrix/plan.md\n\n=== baseline exists ===\napc000.json\napc100.json\napc300.json\nnsys_apc000.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc000.sqlite\n\n=== current measurements ===\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc000.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc100.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300_metrics.json\n\n=== nsight profile ===\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_nsys_apc300.nsys-rep","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4e113b8-a396-45cc-8e86-654a475f0e59","uuid":"39a9725c-cc4a-4577-8abf-2a03b7ac9701","timestamp":"2026-04-16T13:30:21.749Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-16-1430-column-batched-ntt-for-rs-code-matrix\n\nImprove the NTT memory access efficiency in `rs_code_matrix` by processing columns in L2-cache-sized batches instead of all columns simultaneously. The current `batch_ntt` processes all ~53K columns (at APC 300) in a single call, creating a 3.4GB working set that far exceeds the RTX 4090's 72MB L2 cache. This forces every NTT butterfly stage to read from DRAM at large strides, achieving only ~30% of peak bandwidth. By splitting the NTT into batches of ~1000 columns (~64MB per batch, fitting in L2), the second NTT stage reads data that's still L2-resident from the first stage, potentially doubling effective bandwidth. This improvement disproportionately helps APC 300 (short columns, 64KB each, excellent L2 reuse) over APC 0 (tall columns, 4MB each, less L2 benefit).\n\n=== plan.md exists ===\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 georg georg 11389 Apr 16 15:30 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-1430-column-batched-ntt-for-rs-code-matrix/plan.md\n\n=== baseline exists ===\napc000.json\napc100.json\napc300.json\nnsys_apc000.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc000.sqlite\n\n=== current measurements ===\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc000.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc100.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300_metrics.json\n\n=== nsight profile ===\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_nsys_apc300.nsys-rep","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
